Subject: Downgrade flux-core strict lints from deny to warn

Origin: DHI-internal (build compatibility shim for the kapacitor package)
Description: Change flux-core's strict-feature lint level from deny to warn so rustc releases newer than the pinned flux release can compile libflux.
Base-Tree: tarball https://proxy.golang.org/github.com/influxdata/flux/@v/v0.201.0.zip sha256:bff4e628fc9346bb908df953b9f2433f392f01709f70149b98dd5aed002c89d9 path=libflux/flux-core
Verify: cmd `patch -p1 --dry-run -d libflux/flux-core -i flux-core-strict-warnings.patch` expect "checking file src/lib.rs"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI build environment shim only)
Drop-When: never: upstream flux keeps deny(warnings) behind its strict feature and the kapacitor package builds that crate with a newer rustc than the flux release was written for

Flux enables the strict feature by default, which turns every rustc warning into a hard error. A compiler newer than the one flux was developed against emits new warnings for unchanged code, so the lint level is lowered to warn while the code is still compiled exactly as upstream wrote it.

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#![cfg_attr(feature = "strict", deny(warnings, missing_docs))]
+#![cfg_attr(feature = "strict", warn(warnings, missing_docs))]
 #![allow(
     clippy::needless_update, //
     clippy::identity_op, // Warns on `1 * YEARS` which seems clearer than `YEARS`
